# Line endings, pinned per launcher rather than repo-wide.
#
# Deliberately no `* text=auto`: that would renormalise every tracked file on
# the next checkout, which is a large and unrelated diff to hide inside a
# Windows-support change.
#
# The two that actually break:
#
#   *.sh with CRLF — a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true (the default the
#   Git for Windows installer recommends) rewrites liffy.sh's endings on
#   checkout. bash then reads the shebang as `/bin/bash\r` and reports
#   "bad interpreter: No such file or directory", which names a file that
#   plainly exists. Anyone running liffy.sh under WSL or Git Bash hits this.
#
#   *.bat with LF — cmd.exe reads batch files line by line as it executes
#   them, and LF-only endings break that badly enough to run the wrong line.
#   liffy.bat is one command today, but pinning it costs nothing.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
